<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran: US launches fresh strikes as hostilities flare again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9427b4259ed39cf5196fe735b1e9c03ce65dc81c782e34c308eef26941ba5d0</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-us-launches-fresh-strikes-as-hostilities-flare-again/a-78655364--98c85ec79ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-us-launches-fresh-strikes-as-hostilities-flare-again/a-78655364?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Explosions were reported in and around the Strait of Hormuz, as well as at an airport in southern Iran. US President Trump described the strikes as "large and powerful." Iran said the US will "regret" its latest attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4993df95a376d0b8c5c20b270fac4f3bcb8baa1ee473a35a79128515db431a6</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--f90029a93fe3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany terminates lease for Berlin's Russian House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d1c365839dfec53ba911308f3e5d88eaaa55a90f82858b519be480e227c925</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945--51d0280fff89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-terminates-lease-for-berlin-s-russian-house/a-73037945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced the termination of the lease for the Russian House in the heart of Berlin. Critics have long said it is a hub for propaganda and espionage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2010330e0c5eaa3fdc93ef1baaf0838f92d7832e9bb14a832645e8e5a870d0f</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--e12594bca2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>War and sanctions deepen Iran's fuel crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41ddfff9cc401177753680930ffe8cb017fbdca63e5794990647635644cec0b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-and-sanctions-deepen-iran-s-fuel-crisis/a-78636429--9b39d3f812c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-and-sanctions-deepen-iran-s-fuel-crisis/a-78636429?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Long lines at fuel stations are spreading across Iran as war damage, import constraints and new US sanctions squeeze supplies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>As glaciers melt, can communities be protected?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:140b5c9b679e4a5cc3a7475df679320ba9dd8b8607cfe9a71873408d05042fbf</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--e5540929272d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b707311b17a3cae23ed3995fa8922aa026b073c50fdfc1ea277e0d5d390f9321</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--5a8297f9dc8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a91d62cd4c3c9b5ed255b7b433b422099aff5c8e09ba8e2f91b27864617a385f</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--d550ab622814.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh weighs the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:221464cce13dafb5f3f4cc6064dbbe380fc4e9e898b90e340570da5f1be1a339</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--cfde85175591.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's center-left SPD is fighting for survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8e466ce3f1973c3d564e0212073a72f73442b767ab1255f3048034a098325fa</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-center-left-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448--26e37b15aa4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-center-left-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Social Democratic Party is sinking ever deeper into crisis. Voters are turning away, while unrest is growing within its grassroots ranks. Will upcoming state elections accelerate the party's downward spiral?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood: Death toll tops 1,000 as rescue continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:653871d3ee6617c4f95e6aed04f316dffe54afbaf0fdc26874c0113277ec83b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460--9fc4d6386c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities say 4,000 people remain unaccounted for as rescue teams with search dogs comb through mud, rocks and debris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:492e143425fea3003e226b18c17f48dad82dd5c6def39f684d0c7375ae5013ef</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--accd083c93a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Explosive devices found near power plant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6c4a161d9af27cd0cae5d9dea00d33992494e7c0ec063e2342e29d761c17eb7</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741--ea7672909059.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police say they found unconventional explosive and incendiary devices near the Jänschwalde power plant in Brandenburg. Meanwhile, Germany's top diplomat says Algeria could become an important supplier of gas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says it will return to ceasefire if US does</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bcb4de8362c0ddb32e6fc40487e0520cac1282c1873594a92deefd6e4a02b91</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-says-it-will-return-to-ceasefire-if-us-does/a-78586314--217c7ae90d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-says-it-will-return-to-ceasefire-if-us-does/a-78586314?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking on the sidelines of the SCO summit in Kyrgyzstan, Iran's president Pezeshkian called on the US to return to the terms of an interim ceasefire deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02bec135a6ce53d6399b2f65c2926d8cf25291ebaf1328cc8513c183ce718727</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--1fda7d22e067.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Times Square stabbing in NYC leaves 1 dead, assailant killed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5c60c529420c1c6001b6362bd3dfb068af76a527ff8028bf8a21916314910a8</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T07:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/times-square-stabbing-in-nyc-leaves-1-dead-assailant-killed/a-78582543--6978ea3f2c9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/times-square-stabbing-in-nyc-leaves-1-dead-assailant-killed/a-78582543?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A woman armed with two kitchen knives killed one person and wounded another in New York City's Times Square before police fatally shot her. Authorities said the attack was random and unprovoked.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia threatens 'devastating' Baltic response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86294f9d264dff05e1e4735d59be712c506ba367950b33aad92d66ea94879112</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421--7e6d420347ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Any escalation in the Baltic region will lead to a significant response, Moscow said. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ulrich Siegmund wants to make Saxony-Anhalt a model for AfD rule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:341a80ed5dc3232e317b2a15c4a7c93048a2b8821dd94f7c8a33dc073aeac4e5</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:28:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ulrich-siegmund-wants-to-make-saxony-anhalt-a-model-for-afd-rule/a-78579499--24128051ff3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ulrich-siegmund-wants-to-make-saxony-anhalt-a-model-for-afd-rule/a-78579499?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD's lead candidate Ulrich Siegmund aims to turn his small federal state into a blueprint for right-wing extremist politics across Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Tupac Shakur murder trial: Duane 'Keffe D' Davis guilty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c03930178b7aa727be13253d8b768eaa172beef2e3715df238e2ddbe6f02a175</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T00:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tupac-shakur-murder-trial-duane-keffe-d-davis-guilty/a-78581756--4c1e638bfbaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tupac-shakur-murder-trial-duane-keffe-d-davis-guilty/a-78581756?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The jury reached a verdict in less than three hours in a case that had been unsolved for nearly 30 years. Davis was convicted of murder with the use of a deadly weapon and could be sentenced to life in prison.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court allows Trump ballroom project to proceed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54d3e859324a43e84f165592a76c0a6eb0238aed6928beceadc68e7a46d926ff</id><updated>2026-09-01T19:27:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-31